TYPES.md §3.7, §12.1 (DECISIONS 226): the parameters and result of a method written in a public variant's body outside any case are exposed like a case's methods; E2111 at each type expression naming a local type.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local enum Cut { round, square }

local record Stone {
  n: Int
}

/// A shape.
variant Shape {
  /// A ring.
  ring {
    /// Its size.
    size: Int
  }
  /// A bar.
  bar

  /// The stone for a cut.
  fn stone(self, at: Cut) -> Stone? { return none }
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E2111]  a/a.canon:20:22
  Shape is public but exposes the local type Cut: make Cut public or Shape local

error[E2111]  a/a.canon:20:30
  Shape is public but exposes the local type Stone: make Stone public or Shape local

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
